From: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:51:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1-asus-zenbook-a14: Mark the EC reset gpio
 as reserved
References: bsc#1012628
Patch-mainline: 7.3.6
Git-commit: 48213677c9173680de328785768ea56315bfdd53

[ Upstream commit 48213677c9173680de328785768ea56315bfdd53 ]

GPIO 65 from TLMM is used by the embedded controller as its reset line.

On some devices, toggling the embedded controller reset line makes the
device not power up at all, unless the battery is unplugged.

So reserve it in order to prevent Linux from requesting or
reconfiguring it.

Fixes: 6516961352a1 ("arm64: dts: qcom: Add support for X1-based Asus Zenbook A14")
Signed-off-by: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260922-dts-qcom-hamoa-reserve-ec-reset-gpio-v3-10-fde7f8a53382@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Andersson <bjorn.andersson@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Jiri Slaby <jslaby@suse.cz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-asus-zenbook-a14.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-asus-zenbook-a14.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-asus-zenbook-a14.dtsi
index 59cbbfbce490..8eb4c045b58a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-asus-zenbook-a14.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-asus-zenbook-a14.dtsi
@@ -1274,6 +1274,7 @@ wcd_tx: codec@0,3 {
 
 &tlmm {
 	gpio-reserved-ranges = <44 4>,  /* SPI11, TZ Protected */
+			       <65 1>,  /* EC reset */
 			       <90 1>;	/* Unknown, TZ Protected */
 
 	cam_indicator_en: cam-indicator-en-state {
-- 
2.56.1

